# Keep POSIX shell scripts LF even when checked out on Windows (Git for
# Windows defaults to autocrlf=true): a CRLF shebang line breaks them under
# WSL and Git Bash, which is the shell Claude Code runs hooks through there.
*.sh          text eol=lf
*.py          text eol=lf
test/mock/ossprey text eol=lf

# Batch files need CRLF: cmd.exe mis-parses labels and `goto` in LF-only
# files, which would silently break the hook shim and the mock CLI.
*.cmd         text eol=crlf
*.bat         text eol=crlf

# PowerShell reads either; normalise to LF in the repo, native in the tree.
*.ps1         text
*.json        text
*.md          text
